/target
.env
*.log
__pycache__/

# tools/* are each their own standalone [workspace] (never a member of the root one -- see
# tools/protogen/Cargo.toml), so their build output lands in their own target/, not the root one.
/tools/*/target

# script/perf run's output (crates/logit-perf, docs/adr/load-test-harness.md) -- deliberately
# untracked: a results file records one machine's numbers at one commit, not something to commit.
/perf/results/

# script/vm build's stashed binaries (docs/adr/disposable-azure-perf-vm.md's "Multiple sources,
# one VM" section) -- same reasoning as /perf/results/ above, and just as important to exclude:
# left untracked, an unbuilt-until-now perf/bins/ makes `git status --porcelain` report the
# checkout dirty from the first `script/vm build` on, which poisons LOGIT_PERF_GIT_DIRTY in every
# results file `script/perf run` writes afterward on that same checkout.
/perf/bins/
